StorageWorks FDDI Server

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Based on industry-leading Alpha technology integrated with StorageWorks
   modular design

o  Integrated with OpenVMS AXP Storage Management Services

o  Provides advanced, scalable functionality and a complete range of OpenVMS
   AXP data security features

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

StorageWorks FDDI Servers combine industry-leading Alpha technology with
StorageWorks' modular design to meet the storage and I/O requirements of
large FDDI-based VMScluster systems. The new FDDI server family extends the
StorageWorks line with both standard and highly available servers that
support a wide range of StorageWorks solid state disk, magnetic disk, tape,
optical library, and loader devices for configuring FDDI storage solutions
to meet a broad range of application demands.

StorageWorks FDDI Servers provide connectivity to FDDI network environments,
but they do much more than a controller card solution. They provide complete
storage solutions, including connectivity, investment protection via future
upgrades, and complete storage management functionality.

StorageWorks FDDI Servers come in two models: the HS111 for basic FDDI
connectivity and central storage management; and the HS121 for high
availability fault tolerant systems.

BENEFITS

o  Capability for onboard storage management -- The full range of OpenVMS
   AXP storage management tools can be utilized to make either StorageWorks
   FDDI Server model a truly managed storage server. Because these storage
   management utilities actually execute in the server processor, they not
   only have minimal impact on applications, but they also significantly
   reduce I/O traffic on the FDDI bus.

o  Data security via block protection -- As full VMScluster members, the
   servers provide a complete range of OpenVMS AXP data security features
   that block I/O services to hosts. I/O services are restricted to other
   members of the same VMScluster system. Low-level (non-file) I/O is
   restricted to privileged users and provides full protection of the
   OpenVMS AXP file system, including access control by individual user if
   required.

o  Data security via physical redundancy - The HS121 server provides
   complete redundancy of all power sources and data paths to deliver full
   protection against any single component failure. It includes redundant
   server processors, two paths to every storage device, and redundant power
   and cooling. Expansion options are available as add-on components for the
   HS110 and HS121 models.

o  StorageWorks modularity - Since StorageWorks FDDI Servers support a wide
   range of StorageWorks components, storage subsystems can be custom
   configured to meet virtually any application need now, and easily
   upgraded when new technology is available.

o  Ease of use - Each StorageWorks FDDI Server ships from the factory with
   the OpenVMS AXP operating system installed and preconfigured for use as a
   storage server in a VMScluster system. Installation consists of setting
   the server up for the specific storage device configuration (cluster
   identifiers) and installing any optional storage management software.

o  Distance - For users requiring cluster connections beyond 90 meters, the
   current Computer Interconnect (CI) limitation, FDDI network technology
   can currently be connected up to 40 kilometers.

o  Connectivity - The OpenVMS AXP operating system supports up to 96 nodes
   in a single VMScluster system versus a maximum of 32 nodes in a CI
   cluster.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The StorageWorks FDDI Servers are available now through Digital's business
partners and sales offices. Options for the servers will be available as of
January 16, 1995; complementary products are available now.

