SERVICES

Basic or DECservice maintenance agreements, and Media and Documentation
Distribution Service (MDDS) are recommended.

TECHNICAL DATA

The HS1xx family of servers are shipped with OpenVMS AXP V6.1-1H2 installed.
Digital recommends that all FDDI server configurations incorporate the I14Y
Patch Kit. Note, however, that the I14Y Patch Kit must either be installed
on all members of a VMScluster or on none of them. Partial installations
will not function correctly. The I14Y Patch Kit (numbers: AXPSHAD02_061 for
Alpha; VAXSAHD03_061 for VAX) is not available for OpenVMS AXP V1.5.

The following cluster configurations are allowed (see VMScluster
Software for OpenVMS AXP V6.1 SPD for further details):

o  Warranted support: Mixed architecture clusters running OpenVMS V6.1
   (Alpha and VAX)
o  Migration support (1):
   - Alpha-only VMSclusters running OpenVMS AXP V6.1 and OpenVMS AXP V1.5 -
     Mixed-architecture VMSclusters running OpenVMS AXP V6.1 and OpenVMS VAX
     V5.5-2
   - Mixed-architecture VMSclusters running OpenVMS AXP V6.1 and OpenVMS
     VAX V6.0

(1)  Migration support means that Digital has qualified two versions for use
     together in configurations that are migrating in a staged fashion to a
     higher version of OpenVMS or to Alpha software. Digital will respond to
     problem reports submitted about these configurations. However, in
     exceptional cases, Digital may recommend that the user move to a
     warranted configuration as part of the solution.



