TOUCHplus Integrated Solutions From Data Concepts, Inc.

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides touch screen capability for users of Digital's X terminal (VXT),
   OpenVMS (VAX or Alpha), ULTRIX, or DEC OSF/1 applications

o  Supports monitors between 15 and 21 inches in size and all major sensor
   technologies, including capacitive, infrared, resistive, and surface
   acoustical wave (SAW)

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

TOUCHplus is an integrated software and hardware product that can be
customized to facilitate the use (or learning) of any business, healthcare,
nanufacturing, pharmaceutical, financial or kiosk application. Available
exclusively through Data Concepts, Inc., TOUCHplus is 100 percent compatible
with a one-button mouse application.  A companion product, KBplus, will
allow applications to function without modification as if originally written
for touch. KBplus transforms any application into a touch application by
providing on-screen, user-definable keyboards with an associated macro or
script that corresponds to each button. This capability eliminates the need
for a keyboard and mouse.

Designed for multi-tasking, multi-user systems, TOUCHplus features a
consistent interface to all major sensor technologies, which enables users
to select the technology that best fits their application and environment.
Users can wear gloves or use any stylus with all resistive sensors, infrared
sensors, or DECtouch technologies. A soft stylus or glove will work with
surface acoustical wave (SAW) technology. Thin surgical gloves will work
with capacitive technology.

To ensure touch screen capability in abusive environments, TOUCHplus
supports sensors that are accepted in environments that have high
temperature, high humidity, dust and contaminants, as well as Class 100
clean rooms. TOUCHplus integrated solutions are also offered in NEMA 12,
NEMA 4, and NEMA 4X enclosures outfitted with resistive and capacitive
sensors. These enclosures are available in a variety of configurations,
depending on the application.

TOUCHplus can be integrated with most monitors and select flat panel
monitors. In addition, TOUCHplus supports multi-headed monitor applications.

BENEFITS

o  Enhances user productivity by making terminals easier to use

o  Eliminates the need for mouse and/or keyboard in harsh or industrial
   environments

o  Enables users to select the sensor technology that best fits their
   application and environment

o  Provides configuration flexibility

o  Cost effective

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

TOUCHplus is available on now all Digital platforms, including Alpha systems
running the OpenVMS and DEC OSF/1 operating systems. A Windows NT version is
scheduled for release in January 1995.

Turnkey VR320 solutions include TOUCHplus software driver, 19-inch color
monitor, touch sensor of choice, and integration. Monitor retrofits are also
available and include TOUCHplus software driver, touch sensor of
choice, and integration. Quantity discounts are available. Call Data
Concepts, Inc. for additional information.

