DECnet/OSI V6.0 for OpenVMS VAX and AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  DECnet and OSI applications running over TCP/IP transports

o  Expanded naming options

o  Graphical network management interface

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECnet/OSI V6.0 allows DECnet and OSI applications to run over DECnet, OSI,
and TCP/IP transports -- without modification. Network managers can now
consolidate their network backbones without having to rewrite their existing
applications. It is also easier to install and manage than ever before.

DECnet/OSI V6.0 is a major functional release of the network software based
on the Digital Network Architecture. It provides the ability for network
managers to choose their network transport and network naming service
without having to modify their existing network applications. All licensed
DECnet applications, along with user-written and third-party DECnet
applications, can be run over NSP (DECnet transport protocol), CLNS or CONS
(OSI transport protocols), or TCP/IP transports. OSI applications, such as
FTAM, VT, X.400 and X.500, can be run over the OSI protocols or TCP/IP. The
ability to run these applications over TCP/IP is based on an extension to
RFC 1006, currently available from the IETF as an Internet Draft. Through
the use of open interfaces, DECnet/OSI V6.0 allows for the use of any TCP/IP
protocol stack available on OpenVMS systems.

Name service choices have also been expanded. DECnet/OSI for OpenVMS systems
can now access naming information stored in a larger local name service (now
supporting up to 100,000 nodes per system), DECdns software, or DNS/bind.
Also, NCL is now easy to use through the implementation of a Motif based
graphical network management interface.

DECnet/OSI V6.0 continues to preserve existing investments in network
hardware and applications. It is DECnet software plus OSI and is therefore
fully compatible with DECnet Phase IV. Because the Phase IV protocols have
been preserved in DECnet/OSI V6.0, existing DECnet applications will run
unchanged on a DECnet/OSI system. DECnet/OSI and DECnet Phase IV systems
coexist transparently in a single network.

BENEFITS

o  DECnet and OSI applications over TCP/IP -- Existing applications will run
   unmodified over DECnet, OSI, or TCP/IP network backbones.

o  Expanded naming options -- Choice of a local database containing up to
   100,000 nodes, DECdns software, or DNS/bind.

o  Graphical network management interface -- Improved access to network
   management information and commands. The graphical interface is an
   easy-to-use implementation of NCL that allows management of both
   DECnet/OSI and remote DECnet Phase IV systems.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECnet/OSI V6.0 for OpenVMS systems will be available on the Consolidated
CD-ROM in January 1995.

A separate TCP/IP protocol stack is required to use the new DECnet over IP
features. DECnet/OSI V6.0 has been tested with the TCP/IP products from
Digital Equipment Corporation, Process Software, TGV, Inc., and the
Wollongong Group.

A DECnet/OSI license gives the owner the right to use either DECnet/OSI
software or DECnet Phase IV on OpenVMS systems. The DECnet/OSI license is
frequently included as part of VAX and Alpha system packages. Users who
purchase those system packages will receive the new V6.0 license. However, a
DECnet/OSI license is not included with all systems. If this is the case,
users must purchase new licenses.

The End System license provides the right to use the base DECnet and OSI
protocol stacks, FTAM, VT, DECdns Clerk, DECdts, X.25 Access, and network
management. The Extended Function license provides all functions in the End
System plus the OSI application gateways, cluster alias, and on VAX
platforms, the DECdns server.

Update Licenses

Users who already own a DECnet/OSI license need an update license to move to
V6.0. An update license can be obtained by directly purchasing the license
(price is about 30 percent of new license price) or as part of an existing
License Subscription Service.

All DECnet and DECnet/OSI owners must purchase the update license or receive
the rights to use V6.0 as part of the License Subscription Services.
Previous purchase of DECnet or DECnet/OSI software does not convey the right
to use new software versions.

Documentation is provided on the CD-ROM. Hardcopy documents are also
available. New features for this release have been documented in the Release
Notes.

