ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator and Software Developer's Kit

HIGHLIGHTS

o  First release of ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator and ManageWORKS
   Software Developer's Kit

o  Upgrade to the ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator for PATHWORKS
   ManageWORKS users

o  Easy and cost effective way to manage PC networks and workgroups

o  First Windows PC based management platform to combine distributed SNMP
   based network management with multi-vendor PC LAN network operating
   system administration

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator for Windows offers an effective,
affordable solution to the PC LAN management challenge. Running on a single
PC under Windows, ManageWORKS software provides an open standards-based,
network administration framework that lets administrators manage Novell,
Microsoft, IBM, or Digital LANs concurrently.

With ManageWORKS software, a single administrator can perform all of the
management tasks necessary to keep multiple PC LANs running smoothly, using
a graphical overview of their entire LAN (and WAN) landscape. Through
support for the Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) standard,
ManageWORKS software incorporates networking interconnect devices like
bridges, hubs, routers, and switches into the environment. The result is a
powerful, centralized command of the entire environment.

ManageWORKS software uses a modular, open systems paradigm. It lets
administrators create a single, easy-to-use desktop network management
system by allowing third party applications to be added to ManageWORKS
software.

Some of the innovative features of the ManageWORKS product include the
following:

o  Using the point-and-click, drag-and-drop ManageWORKS interface,
   administrators can manage all aspects of PC networks. For example,
   administrators can manage user accounts, groups, file services, print
   services, as well as configure LAN Manager domains (V2.X) and NetWare
   volumes and directories (V3.11 or earlier or V4.X in binary compatibility
   mode). They can also monitor and manage network interconnect devices via
   SNMP from anywhere on a connected LAN network.

o  ManageWORKS SNMP management allows the administrator to monitor and
   actively manage all the network components and connections, over TCP/IP,
   from the same easy-to-use graphical ManageWORKS framework. The specific
   functionality includes basic configuration and monitoring, autodiscovery
   and autolayout of the network (including the wide-area network for IP
   devices), and a Management Information Base (MIB) browser and enrollment
   application, along with a large selection of leading equipment vendors'
   MIBS.

o  The ManageWORKS console application runs on a single Windows PC connected
   to a LAN. It does not require dedicated server hardware, software, or
   special third party databases. This out-of-the-box management lets
   administrators get started immediately. It can run on an inexpensive
   386/33 MHz PC with only 8 Mbytes of memory or on a laptop for mobile
   network troubleshooting.

o  The ManageWORKS viewer provides a structured way for administrators to
   interact with managed objects, whether made of a single object or a group
   or collection of objects. A hierarchy of objects allows the administrator
   to navigate from one level of the network to the next.

o  ManageWORKS customization features give administrators the flexibility to
   centralize, distribute, and tailor network management tasks at any level
   of the organization. For example, the console can be configured to
   automatically display selected objects and a list of tasks used daily.
   This can save time because it streamlines LAN administration.

o  Unlike bundled LAN management solutions provided by PC and LAN operating
   systems vendors, administrators (and developers) are not tied down to a
   single network operating system technology, or denied interconnectivity
   to enterprise-level management systems such as NetView 6000.
   Interoperability with the industry-leading TCP/IP protocol stacks (FTP
   Software, NetManage, Novell LAN WorkPlace, and PATHWORKS products) allows
   PC LAN administrators to pass trapped SNMP events to NetView 6000.

o  ManageWORKS software is the first OLE-2 capable console on the market. It
   allows users to create a variety of new objects, icons, or documents
   using OLE-2 office applications, such as word processors, spreadsheets,
   and graphics programs. These objects can be linked or embedded into
   ManageWORKS software. They can be displayed as an icon or viewed in their
   own window. Editing these objects is now provided through in-place
   activation of the original application.

o  ManageWORKS components in languages other than English are available on
   the CD-ROM media included with these products. The languages included are
   French, Italian, German, Czech, Swedish, and Spanish.

To help developers and administrators take advantage of the opportunity to
expand these capabilities even further, Digital is introducing the
ManageWORKS Software Developer's Kit. The kit gives software developers
everything they need to develop ManageWORKS object management modules. It
allows new and existing Windows based management applications to be
incorporated within the ManageWORKS framework and provides a single network
view. The Software Developer's Kit includes the ManageWORKS console and
application programming interfaces (APIs), as well as ManageWORKS
programming libraries, documentation, sample C and C++ OMM, and Windows
based object management module installers.

Today a growing number of independent software developers are offering new
network management applications for the ManageWORKS environment, adding to
ManageWORKS compatible management solutions available from Digital.
Functions already available include asset management such as software and
hardware inventory, automatic software distribution, remote PC configuration
management, server configuration and performance monitoring, and OpenVMS VAX
and AXP cluster management.

BENEFITS

ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator for Windows offers multiple,
heterogeneous network operating system management and network interconnect
device management from a single Windows based PC.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

PATHWORKS Windows clients include the ManageWORKS framework and the
capabilities needed to manage multiple network operating system PATHWORKS
environments today. Two capabilities available in the ManageWORKS Workgroup
Administrator product are also available separately: LAN Manager and NetWare
Administration software. PATHWORKS ManageWORKS software also includes other
functions that are particular to the PATHWORKS product, such as the
Workstation Manager component, which allows PATHWORKS software to be
installed and configured remotely. PATHWORKS ManageWORKS software does not
include the SNMP network management capabilities of the Workgroup
Administrator product.

PATHWORKS V5.1 users that have the prerequisite license can upgrade to the
ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator product at a reduced price, to gain
these added capabilities. Additionally, enhancements made to the LAN Manager
and NetWare administration functions will be available to Workgroup
Administrator users before the next release of PATHWORKS software.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator software and the ManageWORKS
Software Developer's Kit will be available in January 1995.

PATHWORKS users are already familiar with the ManageWORKS framework and the
LAN Manager and NetWare administration functions, as these are provided as
part of the PATHWORKS complete client licenses. Migration licenses that
allow these users to upgrade to the ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator
product, with all the newly added capabilities such as network management,
are also provided.

The ManageWORKS product family is sold as PC-style, shrink-wrapped products,
which include the license, software media (CD-ROM only), and documentation
in a single package. One license is required for each console.

