commercial re-implementation of the ideas behind NCSA's Mosaic product,
using the same principles of point-and-click network navigation. It is
optimized to run over 14.4 kilobit per second modems as well as higher
bandwidth connections, offering substantial performance improvements for the
Internet's World Wide Web. Netscape provides a common graphical user
interface and a common feature set across computers running the Microsoft
Windows, Macintosh, or X Window environments. Netscape also delivers
security features such as encryption and server authentication. It enables
users to take advantage of such commercial services as online publications,
financial services, and interactive shopping.

Netsite Server Product Line

The Netsite server line (Commerce and Communications servers) are ideal for
corporations, publishers, information providers, service providers, and
retailers. These products allow users to easily set up and maintain servers
for distributing information and conducting commercial operations on
networks. Fully compatible with HTTP based clients and servers, the new
Netsite product line offers increased performance by reducing response times
and making efficient use of available processor power and communications
bandwidth. Available for UNIX based platforms, the line includes two
products designed to meet user requirements: the Netsite Communications
Server and the Netsite Commerce Server.

The Netsite Communications Server is for organizations that want to deliver
non-secure multimedia content to various audiences, such as online marketing
materials to existing and potential users, user support information, or
other communications that do not require security. The server can be scaled
to handle heavy loads or be extended to incorporate new features and
functionality. It also provides intuitive, self-documenting configuration
and management scripts for easy setup.

The Netsite Commerce Server, in addition to offering the above features,
enables secure commerce to be conducted over global TCP/IP networks.
Netscape Communications' incorporation of RSA Data Security technology
provides encryption, which creates a secure channel to prevent anyone from
tapping into the network; and authentication, which uses a digital signature
to verify the legitimacy of the client. The Netsite Commerce Server is
designed for online transactions and electronic data exchange, enabling
users to feel secure sending sensitive information over networks.

BENEFITS

o  Continuous document streaming, enabling users to interact with documents
   while they are still being downloaded rather than waiting for the entire
   document to load.

o  Multiple, simultaneous network accesses, allowing several documents or
   images to be downloaded simultaneously.

o  Embedded support for the JPEG and GIF image format.

o  Netsite and Netscape products running on DEC OSF/1 platforms eliminate
   delays when serving requests or loading graphics. The Alpha system with
   Netscape's products produces the fastest World Wide Web server and
   browser combination on the market.

o  Provides a consistent look and feel across all Netscape clients
